  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "R6: orchestrator/scout_evidence.py \u2014 scout objectives, reusable-evidence check before launching a scout, structured finding validation and scout telemetry (AP P7, P8)",
  "spec": "Why: scouts are spawned by mcp.spawn_scout -> spawn.run_worker with a packet (spawn.py:513-534) that recalls memory titles but nothing checks whether memory, earlier bus scout results or the code graph already answer the question; objectives exist only as free text; results follow the prompt schema {findings:[{claim, evidence, confidence, provenance}], open_questions, ...} with no relevance or unresolved-uncertainty fields and no overlap measurement (AP P7/P8; brief P4). Today two audit scouts cost 2 USD and one failed on budget re-reading files.\nWhat: new pure module orchestrator/scout_evidence.py (MCP wiring and prompt edits are separate tasks).\n- OBJECTIVES = (\"implementation-map\", \"dependency-map\", \"architecture\", \"test-surface\", \"failure-history\", \"security-context\", \"migration-impact\", \"API-consumers\"); normalize_objective(text) -> objective or None (case/dash tolerant).\n- reuse_check(question, *, objective=None, root=STATE, max_age_days=14, min_hits=2, head_sha=None, git=None) -> {\"sufficient\", \"hits\": [{id, title, date, layer, age_days, fresh, reason}], \"reason\", \"objective\"}. Evidence sources via the memory recall module loaded like spawn.memory_recall (layers notes, bus, graph): notes and graph hits are fresh when age_days <= max_age_days; a bus hit (earlier scout result) is fresh only when its task result exists AND (packet_meta.base is unknown OR no path in its scope moved between packet_meta.base and head_sha, using gitutil.moved_paths with the injectable git callable); stale hits never count toward sufficiency, so stale evidence cannot suppress scouting. sufficient = fresh hits >= min_hits.\n- normalize_findings(result) -> list of {\"finding\", \"source\", \"confidence\", \"relevance\", \"unresolved\", \"needs_challenge\"} from a scout result dict in either the prompt schema (claim/evidence/confidence/provenance/open_questions) or the new one; needs_challenge = confidence < 0.7; drops entries without a source; returns [] for malformed input.\n- overlap(findings_a, findings_b) -> {\"jaccard_sources\", \"duplicate_count\"} on normalized source paths (path without line numbers).\n- orthogonal(objectives) -> {\"ok\": bool, \"duplicates\": [...]} for a planned scout set.\n- record_decision(*, question, objective, considered, launched, skipped_reason, hits, task_id=None) -> row appended with bus.log_run(role=\"scout_decision\", ...) including considered, launched, skipped_reason, objective, n_hits; record_use(task_id, used_by) -> bus.log_run(role=\"scout_use\", ...). Tokens come from the scout's own run row.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_scout_evidence.py::test_fresh_duplicate_evidence_marks_scout_unnecessary \u2014 two fresh note hits answering the question yield sufficient True and reason names the hits",
    "tests/test_scout_evidence.py::test_orthogonal_objectives_allowed_and_duplicates_flagged \u2014 orthogonal(['implementation-map','test-surface']) ok True; a repeated objective is listed in duplicates",
    "tests/test_scout_evidence.py::test_normalize_findings_produces_structured_entries_and_flags_low_confidence \u2014 a prompt-schema result yields finding, source, confidence, relevance, unresolved and needs_challenge True for confidence 0.5",
    "tests/test_scout_evidence.py::test_stale_bus_evidence_does_not_suppress_scouting \u2014 a bus scout hit whose scope moved since its packet base is fresh False and sufficient stays False with min_hits 1",
    "tests/test_scout_evidence.py::test_record_decision_logs_considered_and_skipped \u2014 record_decision writes a runs row with role scout_decision carrying considered, launched False, skipped_reason and objective"
  ],
